# A mention of a Structure is not expanded (the author 2026-11-11, LMX_blog/2026-11-11.md#known-name-not-expanded; plan
# M11 5a): `Struct1: Struct2` gives Struct1 one atom, Struct2, and a path through it reads the field of Struct2 itself.
# Data is read whole, so the mention may stand above the declaration of Struct2.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
# The path is read in the code of main (in_code) and from the root through main\data (seen); the data part of main is
# read whole as well.
sub: main () (
    Struct1: Struct2
    Struct2:
        int: v 4
    int: in_code 0
)
    in_code := Struct1\Struct2\v
main()
int: seen main\data\Struct1\Struct2\v
int: seen_in_code main\data\in_code
